// Analyzed file list for tasks/verilog_ethernet_mac_datapath.
//
// Read by two consumers, which is why one list holds every source:
//   * lists/tc_elab.tcl:  analyze -sv12 -f lists/tc_elab.files
//   * taskdefs.slang_args, which filters it into tc_elab.files.slang for the
//     local Slang gate and the design map.
//
// v5/round.py appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker at the
// end, so ORDER MATTERS and the file must end with a newline: the upstream RTL
// comes first, then the formal top that instantiates it, then the candidate
// targets that bind into the formal top, and a worker's file must come last so
// it can reference anything above it.
//
// Paths are relative to the package root -- the drivers `cd $task_root` before
// sourcing tc_elab.tcl, and `slang` is run from there too.
//
// No `+incdir+` and no `+define+`. verilog-ethernet's RTL is self-contained
// Verilog 2001: not one of the eighteen files below has an `include or reads a
// macro it does not define itself.  Every file carries its own
// ``default_nettype none`` / ``resetall`` pair, so the single-unit compile
// order below cannot leak a directive from one file into the next.

// ---- upstream verilog-ethernet, byte-identical --------------------------
//      github.com/alexforencich/verilog-ethernet @ 77320a94 (2025-02-27)
//
//      lib/axis/rtl/ -- the AXI-Stream library, leaves first
rtl/axis/priority_encoder.v
rtl/axis/arbiter.v
rtl/axis/sync_reset.v
rtl/axis/axis_register.v
rtl/axis/axis_pipeline_register.v
rtl/axis/axis_adapter.v
rtl/axis/axis_fifo.v
rtl/axis/axis_async_fifo.v
rtl/axis/axis_async_fifo_adapter.v
//      rtl/ -- the MAC and the Ethernet frame layer
rtl/verilog_ethernet/lfsr.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/axis_gmii_rx.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/axis_gmii_tx.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_mac_1g.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_mac_1g_fifo.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_axis_rx.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_axis_tx.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_demux.v
rtl/verilog_ethernet/eth_arb_mux.v

// ---- task-authored formal top: the frame source, the bounded link stalls,
//      the whole rx -> split -> demux -> fifos -> arb -> rejoin -> tx chain
//      and the monitor receiver on the transmitted link -------------------
ft/verilog_ethernet_mac_datapath_ft.sv

// ---- task-authored oracle, candidate targets and covers.  LAST: a `bind`
//      must be analyzed after the module it binds into ---------------------
sva/targets_verilog_ethernet_mac_datapath.sv
